      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Luigi.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 5, power rating 13 → a level 4 Ranger player-character sheet for <strong>955 BF</strong> (Luigi, the second brother; never above the ledger level — a past self holds no more experience than the present one). Before the Poltergust. Sports appearances, heroic support, the brother behind the brother — already afraid often, already going anyway.. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Reluctant Ghostbuster</strong> — Mushroom Kingdom / Mages' Guild (Contractor)</p><p>Status: Active — recovered alive from Bowser's lava-moat tunnels, treated at Dr. Toad's Star Hill Clinic, and under a two-week rest order; Mario remains absent.; as of 2 Aethel, 1035 BF reported — unverified — to be in the clinic's 'private wing, high security, consciousness fluxing', while something wearing his clothes stood outside in three copies</p><p>Luigi is the reluctant ghostbuster, the brother left behind by every heroic story that needed Mario in front, and the man whose history now carries the unresolved shadow of Mr. L, Guild contracts, haunted technology, medical testimony, and a disappearance mystery too large to fit inside the word sidekick. Waluigi finds Luigi infuriating, sympathetic, suspicious, brave, evasive, and extremely bad at choosing restful employment. The Poltergust is not just a vacuum; it is Luigi's proof that fear can be weaponized into duty. The Garden Above the Fire confirms that Luigi survived the lava-falls aftermath, recalled the line 'The star is not lost. Find the garden above the fire,' and reached Dr. Toad's clinic alive — still wounded, still asking for Mario, but no longer missing in the compound tunnels.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Hammer</strong> — “This is why Luigi's records are uneven: sports appearances, ghost incidents, heroic support, then sudden gaps, Mr. L references, Guild contracts, and medical testimony.”</li><li><strong>Green Fireball</strong> — “This is why Luigi's records are uneven: sports appearances, ghost incidents, heroic support, then sudden gaps, Mr. L references, Guild contracts, and medical testimony.”</li><li><strong>Scuttle Jump</strong> — “A person defined as the second brother can disappear in plain sight because institutions file him under support, not center.”</li><li><strong>The Second Brother</strong> — “A person defined as the second brother can disappear in plain sight because institutions file him under support, not center.”</li><li><strong>Afraid Often</strong> — “Luigi is afraid often.”</li><li><strong>Startles</strong> — “He shakes, complains, startles, and then points the Poltergust at the ghost anyway.”</li><li><strong>Sports Appearances</strong> — “This is why Luigi's records are uneven: sports appearances, ghost incidents, heroic support, then sudden gaps, Mr. L references, Guild contracts, and medical testimony.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/luigi</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/luigi/955-bf</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
